Hands one big write to NIM, the model that writes at length, in one call: a whole document, curriculum, tier's cards or tier's quiz. NIM reads your whole chat and your instructions and writes the arguments of the tool you name ({{ tools | join(" or ") }}); code stores them through that tool, whose checks decide what passes. Write the instructions as a brief: what to write in this call and what to draw on. NIM takes some five minutes to start any answer, so a small write (a fix, a few cards, a section added or dropped) you make yourself with the tool. The result shows what NIM wrote and what was stored or refused; fix a refusal yourself with the tool, sending only what changes.
